{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "This trip was sold on an upfront quote. The fare_breakdown records fare_model UPFRONT_QUOTE with quoted_fare_sgd non-null at SGD 28.00, so the price was fixed at booking and POL-RD-02's distance-and-time recomputation does not run at all; POL-RD-11 is the clause that governs the rider's remedy on this trip.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00517"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-11"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.fare_model",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The ledger then charged SGD 67.50 against that SGD 28.00 quote, which is SGD 39.50 more than the upfront price the platform itself set. The charge was assembled from distance (SGD 16.40) and time (SGD 40.50) lines that the upfront contract had already fixed at booking, plus a SGD 6.00 airport surcharge and a SGD 0.80 platform fee. The rider disputes exactly that excess over the quote, and POL-RD-11(a) makes it refundable in full.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00517"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-11"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.charged_over_quote",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-11(a) fixes the refund as charged_total less quoted_fare less the pass-through and statutory lines properly chargeable under POL-RD-09. The only properly chargeable line here is the SGD 6.00 Changi airport surcharge, because this trip ORIGINATES at Changi Airport Terminal 3 (trip_record pickup label 'Changi Airport Terminal 3, Departure Level Door 5'). There are no ERP gantry lines (erp_gantries is empty), no tolls, and a SGD 0.00 waiting-time fee. The refund is therefore 67.50 − 28.00 − 6.00 = SGD 33.50, already a multiple of SGD 0.05.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00517", "EV-TRIP-00517"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-11", "POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.pol_rd_11_remedy",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The entitlement under POL-RD-11(a) is arithmetic on the fare ledger against the price the platform quoted, and it does not depend on establishing a POL-RD-01 deviation. Even if no distance deviation is established on this trip, the rider still recovers the amount by which the platform charged above its own fixed upfront price; POL-RD-11 supplies that remedy and POL-RD-01's threshold test does not displace it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00517"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-11", "POL-RD-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing on the record reduces that figure as a rider-caused detour. The trip's chat_log is empty — message_count 0, messages array empty — so POL-RD-04's rider-instruction exoneration is unavailable: there is no rider message asking for a stop, a waypoint or a particular road, and no waypoint_hint to corroborate one. The driver cannot point to a recorded instruction to justify any part of the charge.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00517"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No external traffic cause is on file either. The traffic_advisory artifact EV-ADVIS-00517-01 is MISSING — its payload is null and its weight_multiplier is 0.0 — so POL-RD-03's comparison (an advisory naming a road the optimal route traverses, with an overlapping validity window, matched by a route that leaves and rejoins the corridor) cannot be run on this record, POL-RD-03 is unavailable, and any 'something external happened' explanation carries no weight under POL-RD-08. The absence is itself citable, and it leaves the POL-RD-11(a) arithmetic untouched.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00517-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-13"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider carries no special corroboration burden. rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d is 0 and rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d_substantiated is 0, so POL-RD-08's condition (4 or more claims in 60 days with 1 or fewer substantiated) does not attach and no corroboration beyond the artifacts already cited is required of this rider.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-00517"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "relies_on": "rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's own account confirms the charge was not the product of any route the rider chose. He states the app crashed mid-trip, that he dropped the rider at the hotel, and that the app 'completed the trip by itself' — 'I didn't choose the amount.' The trip_record corroborates the shape of that account: status COMPLETED, a post-hoc charge at 22:42:00, and zero chat messages. Nothing on the rider's side explains the SGD 39.50 jump from quote to charge, which is precisely why POL-RD-11(a) places that excess back with the rider.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00517", "EV-FARE-00517"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-11"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver-device trace is IMPAIRED, and I disclose that: EV-GPS-00517 carries weight 0.39 with issue codes GPS_GAP (a single 620-second gap from 22:26:30 to 22:36:50) and LOW_COVERAGE (65.6% across the active window). That is exactly the frozen-icon failure the rider describes — the app stopped reporting mid-trip. A telemetry failure on the platform's own side is not the rider's to pay for, and it does not disturb the POL-RD-11(a) figure, which is computed from the fare ledger and the quoted fare and not from the trace.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00517", "EV-FARE-00517"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "max_gap_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 0.39
    }
  ]
}

