      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-00517-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The rider carries the initial burden under POL-RD-08 and must show, citing evidence, an excess meeting the POL-RD-01 threshold measured either from an unimpaired trace or from one of the independent sources POL-RD-07(ii) names. She can show neither: the measured excess is 0.3 km / 1.53%, and the only trace on file is impaired at weight 0.39. The deviation claim therefore fails at the first limb of POL-RD-08 before any exculpatory clause is reached.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-GPS-00517 at weight_multiplier 0.39 but does not name its issue code(s): GPS_GAP, LOW_COVERAGE"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Under POL-GEN-02(2) the confidence in any finding carried by the trace is capped by its weight_multiplier of 0.39, which is below the 0.70 platform-wide escalation floor in POL-RD-10(1). The route question here rests on EV-GPS-00517 alone, so the cap bites and the case escalates automatically; the bundle mean weight is context only and is not the cap.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-GPS-00517 at weight_multiplier 0.39 but does not name its issue code(s): GPS_GAP, LOW_COVERAGE"
    }
  ]
